Chapter: ProbeClosureRelay

 Does the closure have to be BUILT in the tail-recursive definition, or
 merely returned by it? Here the base case calls another definition that
 makes the closure, so the trampoline in the recursive definition targets
 `make-adder` rather than a leaf like `add3`.

 `relayed 47` means what matters is building the closure in a
 tail-recursive definition, not returning one from it. A fault means any
 function-returning tail-recursive definition is affected regardless of
 where the closure comes from, which widens the predicate.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  make-adder : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make-adder (n) = add3 n

  count-relay : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  count-relay (n) = if n == 0 then make-adder 5 else count-relay (n - 1)

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("relayed " & show (((count-relay 3) 20) 22))
  end
